This licence covers the code in this repository only. The generated data and
every data export (the SQLite file, the CSV tables, DATA.md and the published
site's figures) are not under MIT: they are licensed in layers, one per source,
as LICENSE-DATA.md states (ADR 0003, docs/adr/0003-licences-and-impressum.md).

Source material from the Deutscher Bundestag held in this repository is not
under MIT either: the Plenarprotokoll XML files and excerpts, the roll-call
pages and lists, and the MdB-Stammdaten excerpt under tests/fixtures/, and the
names, Redner-IDs, protocol references and quoted wording in the data files
under scripts/ (for example person_corrections.json, reviewed_units.json) and
in docs/. Quelle: Deutscher Bundestag/Bundesrat – DIP (Plenarprotokolle cited
as „BT-PlPr." with their number) and Deutscher Bundestag (bundestag.de, the
roll-call pages and the MdB-Stammdaten). Many test fixtures are shortened or
edited to test one case; they are not the official text. Plenarprotokolle are
amtliche Werke (§ 5 Abs. 2 UrhG); the DIP terms of use
(https://dip.bundestag.de/documents/nutzungsbedingungen_dip.pdf), in particular
no. 5, apply to their reuse as conditions of the source, not as terms we add.
Whether the roll-call excerpts may be held here was asked of the Bundestag on
2026-11-21 (TODOS.md, "Settle the roll-call source for redistribution").
